tion">Content planning, design and scheduling — the rhythm of a recognisable social presence.</figcaption></figure><section class="service-detail section"><div><span class="eyebrow">SOCIAL MEDIA MANAGEMENT</span><h2>From the big picture<br>to the finer details.</h2><div class="service-type-art" aria-hidden="true"><small>NITIKSHAM / SOCIAL-MEDIA-MARKETING</small><strong>Hello.</strong><span>Considered. Connected. Crafted.</span></div></div><div><div class="deliverable reveal"><span>01</span><h3>Social strategy</h3><p>We start with your audience and your goals, then decide what each platform is for — so every post has a job to do, not just a slot to fill.</p></div><div class="deliverable reveal"><span>02</span><h3>Content calendars</h3><p>A planned calendar of posts, stories and reels, built around your business rhythm — launches, seasons, offers and the stories only you can tell.</p></div><div class="deliverable reveal"><span>03</span><h3>Social media graphics</h3><p>Distinctive, on-brand visuals designed in-house, so your feed is recognisable at a glance and consistent with the rest of your brand.</p></div><div class="deliverable reveal"><span>04</span><h3>Campaign content</h3><p>Focused content for launches, festivals and offers — planned, designed and written to work together across your platforms.</p></div><p class="caption">Your project scope, deliverables and timeline are agreed after our first conversation.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>What a managed presence looks like</h2><p>Social media works when it is planned like everything else in your marketing — with a clear idea, a consistent look and a voice people recognise.</p></div><div class="values"><article class="reveal"><span>01</span><h3>Planned, not posted on a whim</h3><p>Every month begins with a content plan: themes, formats and dates agreed in advance, so your feed never scrambles for something to say.</p></article><article class="reveal"><span>02</span><h3>Designed to be recognised</h3><p>Your posts share one visual language — colours, type and layout that match your brand — so followers know it is you before they read the name.</p></article><article class="reveal"><span>03</span><h3>Written in your voice</h3><p>Captions are written in the voice your customers already know, clear and human. Our <a href="/copyright/">copywriting &amp; content</a> team keeps that voice steady across every platform.</p></article><article class="reveal"><span>04</span><h3>Reviewed and adjusted</h3><p>We look at what people respond to and what they ignore, then adjust the plan — more of what works, less of what does not.</p></article></div></section><section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Social media, connected to the rest of your marketing</h2></div><div class="two-copy"><p>A social feed does its best work when it is not on its own. Your posts can point people to a website that is ready for them, support a <a href="/digital-marketing/">digital marketing</a> campaign, or carry the same message as your print and outdoor work — one brand, speaking clearly in every place it appears.</p><p>That is how we plan it. Social media is one part of a wider plan built around your business — the same thinking behind our <a href="/expertise-seo/">SEO</a> and website work, applied to the platforms where your audience spends its time. Whether you sell to customers across India or to buyers around the world, the approach stays the same: say something worth following, and say it consistently.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Social media marketing, answered</h2><p>The questions businesses ask us most before starting a social media plan.</p></div><div class="values"><article class="reveal"><span>01</span><h3>What does your social media marketing service include?</h3><p>Strategy, content planning, graphics, captions and scheduling — the full rhythm of a managed social presence. We agree the platforms, the posting frequency and the themes with you, then design and write the content in-house so it stays on-brand.</p></article><article class="reveal"><span>02</span><h3>Which social media platforms do you manage?</h3><p>We work across the platforms your audience actually uses — including Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn, YouTube and X. If you are unsure where to focus, we recommend the platforms that fit your customers and your goals, rather than trying to be everywhere at once.</p></article><article class="reveal"><span>03</span><h3>Do you create the graphics and captions?</h3><p>Yes. Social graphics are designed in-house and captions are written by our copywriting team, so design and words work together and your feed keeps one consistent voice.</p></article><article class="reveal"><span>04</span><h3>How often will you post for us?</h3><p>Posting frequency is agreed with you at the start and written into your content plan. It depends on your platforms, your audience and your budget — steady and sustainable beats a burst of posts followed by silence.</p></article><article class="reveal"><span>05</span><h3>Can social media marketing work for a small or local business?</h3><p>Yes. Small and local businesses often benefit most, because social media lets you speak directly to the people nearby — your neighbourhood, your city, your region. A clear, regular presence builds familiarity, and familiarity builds trust.</p></article></div></section><section class="new-cta"><span class="eyebrow">GIVE PEOPLE A REASON</span><h2>Start conversations.<br><em>Build connections.</em></h2><p>Create a social presence with a consistent point of view.</p><a class="button" href="/contact-us/">Start a conversation ↗</a></section></main><footer class="new-footer"><div class="footer-grid"><div><a class="wordmark brand-wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Nitiksham home"><img src="<?php echo esc_url(get_template_directory_uri()); ?>/assets/nitiksham-brand.png" alt="Nitiksham — an idea driven agen